@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:1000
@CO	Records for query/strand/unconverted.toml
@CO	query/strand/unconverted.toml -- no conversion chemistry, so every record walks the reference forward and 0x10 says only which way the read was sequenced. The original strand is forward on everything.
@CO	These records carry no aux tag, because the rule reads none. They are the four
@CO	paired layouts and both single-end orientations: the original strand is forward on
@CO	every one of them, which is the point, and only the aligned direction moves.
@CO	Each QNAME is the call the rule must make for that record: "<original>:<aligned>",
@CO	each side forward or reverse, or "unknown". Anything after the first "/" is a label
@CO	for the reader. The test that enforces it is in src/strand_rule.rs.
forward:forward/pe-99	99	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	200	ACGT	IIII
forward:reverse/pe-147	147	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	-200	ACGT	IIII
forward:reverse/pe-83	83	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	-200	ACGT	IIII
forward:forward/pe-163	163	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	200	ACGT	IIII
forward:forward/se-0	0	chr1	101	60	4M	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII
forward:reverse/se-16	16	chr1	101	60	4M	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII
